  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="44">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 44</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="44" corresp="#wit-g-a">Gif deaðscyldig man scriftspæce gyrne, ne wyrne him man æfre.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="44" corresp="#wit-a">Gif deoðscyldig man sriftsprace georne, ne wirne man him æfre.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="44" corresp="#wit-q">Si quis morti dampnatus confessionem facere (habere) desideret, numquam negetur (defendatur) ei.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="44" corresp="#wit-b">Gyf deaðscyldig man scriftspréce gyrne, ne wyrne him nan man næfre.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">Gif deaðscyldig man scriftspæce gyrne, ne wyrne him man æfre.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">If a condemned man desires confession, it shall never be refused him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">If someone sentenced to death desires confession, it shall never be denied to him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">If a condemned man desire confession, it is never to be refused him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn ein Todes schuldiger Mensch Beichte verlangt, werde sie ihm niemals verweigert.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a man condemned to death asks for confession, let it never be refused him.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="342"><ref target="clause:EGu_5">EGu 5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 5</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares EGu 5.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">ibid., 5</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">him man æfre: him nan man næfre B</note>
      </div>
    </body>
